==============================================================================
1. INVENTORY -- what the leg record carries about declined-vs-killed
==============================================================================
Written by batch/driver.py::RunOutcome.to_dict and batch/runner.py::_timeout_row / _crash_row.

row field             shape                                                     reached by scorer   note
status                closed: pass|fail|error|timeout|scope_conflict            YES                 runner writes error/timeout; driver writes pass/fail/scope_conflict
failure_kind          closed: ambiguous_review_scope, contract, crash, llm, ne  YES                 no_reactions is the declared decline; timeout/crash are casualties
stage                 free-ish; 'unknown' on the OUTER kill path                YES                 F-148: 'unknown' means the PARENT could not see, not a pipeline stage
message               free text                                                 YES                 the stated reason. EMPTY is a silence
issue_codes           list of guard/gate codes                                  YES                 an explicit named stop
termination_reason    closed, 7 values: retrieval_exhausted, no_new_claims, bu  NEW in C-110        conditional key; ABSENT on every leg that did not time out
operational_failure   bool                                                      NEW in C-110        is_operational(termination_reason); written by BOTH kill paths under this name
counts                dict; {} on the outer-kill path                           NEW in C-110        {} = NOT MEASURED; {'reactions': 0} = affirmatively none
files                 list; [] on the outer-kill path                           NEW in C-110        F-148 section 3: [] is the signature of a kill with the reserve spent
budget                dict, timeout rows only                                   NO                  GAP -- elapsed/remaining never reach the acceptance leg
budget_unrecorded     str, inner timeout only                                   NO                  GAP
detail                free text, capped                                         NO                  GAP -- the traceback tail never reaches the acceptance leg
warnings              list                                                      NO                  GAP
attempts / retries    DOES NOT EXIST                                            N/A                 F-148 section 5: the artifact needed to exclude retry amplification is the one the kill destroyed

GAPS, NAMED (they belong to F-148, not to this card):
  * `budget` / `budget_unrecorded` / `detail` / `warnings` are on the row
    and are NOT carried onto the acceptance leg. C-110 did not add them:
    none of them separates declined from killed better than the four it did.
  * There is NO attempt or retry record of any kind on ANY row shape. A leg
    that was killed cannot be shown to have retried or not retried.
  * `stage` is 'unknown' on the outer-kill path BY DESIGN. A reader treating
    it as a pipeline stage will mis-diagnose. C-110 does not read `stage`.
  * A row written before termination_reason/operational_failure existed has
    NEITHER key. C-110 treats that as INDETERMINATE, never as clean.

==============================================================================
2. DISCRIMINATION -- the four canonical shapes through the new rule
==============================================================================
declined (the ruling's case)     -> PASS_NEGATIVE_CONTROL
                                    conditions : {'no_reactions_released': True, 'declared_decline_reason': True, 'no_execution_failure': True}
                                    blocked_by : []
timed out (outer kill)           -> NOT_AWARDED
                                    conditions : {'no_reactions_released': True, 'declared_decline_reason': False, 'no_execution_failure': False}
                                    blocked_by : ['execution_failure', 'no_artifacts_preserved', 'no_stated_reason']
empty and silent                 -> NOT_AWARDED
                                    conditions : {'no_reactions_released': True, 'declared_decline_reason': False, 'no_execution_failure': True}
                                    blocked_by : ['no_stated_reason', 'indeterminate_classification']
empty, no artifacts preserved    -> NOT_AWARDED
                                    conditions : {'no_reactions_released': True, 'declared_decline_reason': True, 'no_execution_failure': False}
                                    blocked_by : ['no_artifacts_preserved']

BOTH ARMS of _empty_is_correct, on the pinned gold:
  PMC13231680  is_negative_control=True  relevance=context_only  min_connected=0  -> arm=is_negative_control  status=PASS_NEGATIVE_CONTROL
  PMC12180156  is_negative_control=False  relevance=context_only  min_connected=0  -> arm=context_only_no_minimum_core  status=PASS_NEGATIVE_CONTROL

A relevant paper is not judged by this rule at all:
  PMC12096016  _empty_is_correct=False  record=None
  PMC12452463  _empty_is_correct=False  record=None

OPERATIONAL_TERMINATION_REASONS (D-005, imported not restated): ['budget_exhausted', 'operation_timeout']

